    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0536" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 British Honduras/191</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Osborne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>)<anchor n="67"
                        xml:id="d313-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-22">October 22,
                        1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: You will recall that you
                    were good enough to write to the Ambassador on the 5th August last in regard to
                    the steps taken in the British West Indies to prevent smuggling of liquor into
                    the United States.</p>
                <p>I have now been instructed by Sir Samuel Hoare<anchor n="68" xml:id="d313-f2"/>
                    to inform you that His Majesty’s Government in the United Kingdom greatly
                    appreciate <pb facs="0537" n="435" xml:id="pg435"/> the terms of your letter,
                    and that they remain fully prepared to discuss from time to time with the United
                    States Government in an informal way, any problems which may arise in connection
                    with possible illicit shipments from particular localities.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Osborne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d313-f1" n="67" type="source" xml:id="d313-f1-content">
